Some comments on NH 3.0:

* A nice part of the nopickup switch in the last version of NH was that it
would still pick up money.

* It would be nice if the door character changed to reflect the 
locked/opened/closed state changes.  As it is you can hose yourself by going
to a bum door.  You might argue that only open/closed is valid as that's
all you can 'see' in real life.

* I like all the extra monsters.  It'd be nice if 'tame' animals we marked by
the same highlight that marks the player.  This is especially a problem with
dogs and cats.

On the copyleft;  it seems to me that once software is distributed the way
that Hack has been (essentially public domain) that one cannot impose a 
more restrictive license (you are always free to make something less 
restrictive ;-) any (many, millions?) of opinions on this?

